L''ange Pro Ambassador', 'https://tiktok.com/@katieoliv_hair', null, 18178, 603, 5.43, 10724.02, 'Fashion Accessories', '["Fashion Accessories","Beauty & Personal Care"]', 52, null, null, 'New Lead', 'Anh Tuan (Scraper Bot)', 'Katieocollabs@gmail.com', null, null, null, null, '2026-08-04T06:03:41.620Z', '2026-08-10T05:50:21.363Z', '[]', '["TikTok Scraped","Pickdi TCM Extension","United States","Scraper Enriched","Pickdi TCM Extension (auto-queue)"]', null, 36, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, '[{"id":"7662933638866029854","date":"2026-07-16","thumb":"","title":"These are the rules that I follow and recommend to my clients—but they’re exactly that: my recommendations. 🤍 If you like to go longer than 4 weeks between move-ups and it’s working for you, that’s completely your choice. Every head of hair is different. This is simply the maintenance schedule I recommend to help keep butterfly extensions secure while protecting your natural hair. ✨ My maintenance routine: • Move-up every 4 weeks • Every other maintenance appointment = a full reinstall Why? Because your scalp naturally sheds 75–100 hairs every single day, and those shed hairs become trapped inside the bead. Over time, the section holding your extension isn’t as full as the day it was installed, creating a weaker anchor. A full reinstall removes all of that shed hair and gives your extension a fresh, strong foundation. Healthy installs will always be my priority over the fastest maintenance appointment. Save this for your next maintenance day, and send it to your DIY extension bestie who needs to hear this. 💛 @FullShineHair Store  #ButterflyExtensions #DIYHairExtensions #HairExtensionMaintenance #fullshinehairextentions #haireducation","views":7815,"videoUrl":"https://www.tiktok.com/@katieoliv_hair/video/7662933638866029854","isBranded":false},{"id":"7668507563352165663","date":"2026-07-31","thumb":"","title":"one brush, zero switching 🤍 detangle wet curls AND style them 