🏠home/lifestyle', 'https://tiktok.com/@kelleejoann', null, 3679, 758, 0.88, 25107.4, 'Beauty & Personal Care', '["Beauty & Personal Care","Health","Home Supplies"]', 50, null, null, 'New Lead', 'Anh Tuan (Scraper Bot)', 'kelleesocial@outlook.com', null, null, null, null, '2026-08-04T14:55:24.500Z', '2026-08-05T02:19:47.343Z', '[]', '["TikTok Scraped","Pickdi TCM Extension","United States","Scraper Enriched","Pickdi TCM Extension (auto-queue)"]', null, 524, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, '[{"id":"7661258181233921293","date":"2026-07-11","thumb":"","title":"Replying to @Josephine yaaas🫡🦷 If your gums bleed when you floss, your body is trying to tell you something. It’s a sign of inflammation caused by bacteria sitting under your gums. The good news? Bleeding gums are often reversible with consistency. People think bleeding means they should stop flossing, but it’s actually a sign that you need to floss more consistently. As the bacteria and plaque are removed day after day, the inflammation decreases, and the bleeding usually improves. Yes, traditional string floss is considered the gold standard because it can adapt closely to the shape of each tooth. But here’s what matters most..the best floss is the one you’ll actually use every single day. If floss picks help you build a daily habit, then use floss picks. A consistent flossing routine with floss picks is far better than perfect string floss that’s still sitting unopened in your bathroom drawer. Consistency is what creates healthier gums, not perfection. These are the floss picks I use and love as a dental hygienist.  #floss #flossing #whiterteeth #teethcare #gumdisease","views":447636,"videoUrl":"https://www.tiktok.com/@kelleejoann/video/7661258181233921293","isBranded":false},{"id":"7660663400837532942","date":"2026-07-09","thumb":"","title":"A lot of people have never heard of an oral probiotic, so don’t worry if this is new to you. Unlike regular probiotics that support your gut, oral probiotics are designed specifically for your mouth. They help increase the beneficial bacteria in your oral microbiome, which can help crowd out the harmful bacteria that contribute to tonsil stone buildup, bad breath, and unhealthy or bleeding gums. Think of it as helping your mouth maintain a healthier balance of good bacteria so the bad bacteria have a harder time taking over. I’ve been a dental hygienist for 11 years and this is the oral probiotic that I recommend to all my patients and what my family personally loves and uses.  #oralprobiotics #tonsilstones #tonsil #badbreathtreatment #teethcare","views":74322,"videoUrl":"https://www.tiktok.com/@kelleejoann/video/7660663400837532942","isBranded":false},{"id":"7660156655962836237","date":"2026-07-08","thumb":"","title":"Replying to @anastasiacoconut this is the best comment! You made me laugh! The dental hygienist in me loves that you love the feeling of clean teeth! 😉 but it’s always a great reminder for all of us..Brushing harder doesn’t mean brushing better. Here are some reasons to avoid brushing too hard.. It can cause gum recession. Your gums can slowly pull away from your teeth, exposing sensitive root surfaces. It wears away enamel. Once enamel is gone, it doesn’t grow back. It can make your teeth sensitive to hot, cold, and sweets. It doesn’t remove more plaque. Proper technique is much more effective than using extra force. It can irritate your gums, causing soreness or bleeding. Think of it this way, the Nova Sonic toothbrush has the soft, tapered bristles that gently reach around your gums and teeth, while the 18,000 sonic vibrations break up plaque. Instead of scrubbing, you simply guide the toothbrush and let it do the work. That’s how you get an effective clean while protecting your teeth and gums.  #electrictoothbrush #toothbrush #whiterteeth #brushingteeth #whiteteeth","views":54766,"videoUrl":"https://www.tiktok.com/@kelleejoann/video/7660156655962836237","isBranded":false}]', 