📧Melisza@kensingtongrey.co', 'https://www.tiktok.com/@meliszamcfierce', null, 374400, 48013, 7.74, 117, 'Beauty & Personal Care', '["Beauty & Personal Care","Fashion Accessories","Womenswear & Underwear"]', 96, null, null, 'New Lead', 'Anh Tuan (Scraper Bot)', 'Melisza@kensingtongrey.co', null, null, null, null, '2026-08-06T09:42:52.789Z', '2026-08-07T08:05:10.170Z', '[]', '["TikTok Scraped","File Import (Kalodata_Creator_20260806172324_US.xlsx)","Scraper Enriched","Pickdi TCM Extension (handle-search)","Pickdi TCM Extension (auto-queue)","File Import (Kalodata_Creator_20260807160415_US.xlsx)"]', null, 54, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, '[{"id":"7662103541510720781","date":"2026-07-13","thumb":"","title":"I love a good makeup trend just as much as the next person. Trying new products is fun, and I think trends can be a great way to discover something you genuinely end up loving. But if you’re someone who wears makeup every day, I don’t think you need to feel pressured to keep up with every new launch or viral product. The truth is, a small collection of products that you know work for you will almost always outperform a drawer full of products you barely reach for. A solid foundation, a concealer you trust, a bronzer you love, and a few everyday staples are more than enough to create beautiful makeup over and over again. I’ve realized that building a makeup collection with intention feels so much more rewarding than constantly chasing the next trend. Buy products because they fill a gap in your routine or genuinely make getting ready easier not because the internet convinced you that you need them. Trends come and go, but a thoughtfully curated makeup collection will serve you every single day. This has a balanced, “beauty bestie” feel that fits your content encouraging without making people feel guilty for enjoying trends.","views":370769,"videoUrl":"https://www.tiktok.com/@meliszamcfierce/video/7662103541510720781","isBranded":false},{"id":"7662535709714025741","date":"2026-07-14","thumb":"","title":"There’s something about pink makeup that changes the way you carry yourself. It’s soft without being boring, feminine without feeling overdone, and somehow manages to make you look effortlessly put together even when the rest of life feels a little chaotic. I’ve always believed the best makeup isn’t the kind that completely transforms your face it’s the kind that brings out the version of you that was already there. The colors that make your eyes brighter, your skin look healthier, and your confidence feel just a little quieter, but a whole lot stronger. This look reminded me that sometimes the prettiest makeup isn’t the one that gets the most attention. It’s the one that makes you catch your own reflection, smile for a second, and think, “Yeah… I really like this.” And honestly, that’s more than enough for me. 🌸","views":207521,"videoUrl":"https://www.tiktok.com/@meliszamcfierce/video/7662535709714025741","isBranded":false},{"id":"7665487357843361038","date":"2026-07-22","thumb":"","title":"Brown eyes never needed brighter colors to stand out they just need the right ones. Soft taupes, warm bronzes, rich chocolates, and a touch of champagne create depth, warmth, and that effortless, expensive-looking finish. Sometimes the most timeless looks come from the most neutral palette. If you have brown eyes, consider this your reminder: you don’t have to do the most to make them unforgettable. Save this look for your next makeup day, and let me know if you want more eye-maxxing tutorials. 🤎✨","views":121390,"videoUrl":"https://www.tiktok.com/@meliszamcfierce/video/7665487357843361038","isBranded":false}]', '{"topGender":"Female","genderMale":17,"topCountry":"TEXAS","topAgeGroup":"25-34","genderFemale":83,"ageDistribution":[{"name":"25-34","value":37},{"name":"35-44","value":29},{"name":"45-54","value":16},{"name":"18-24","value":11},{"name":"55+","value":7}],"countryDistribution":[{"name":"TEXAS