’s heart. But when you read Exodus carefully, you discover something important: Pharaoh repeatedly hardened his own heart before God confirmed the path he had chosen. This passage isn’t about God creating evil—it’s about the danger of continually rejecting His voice. Every encounter with God changes us. The question is whether our hearts become softer or harder in response. #BibleStudy #Exodus7 #ChristianTok #HardHeart #Faith","views":18204,"videoUrl":"https://www.tiktok.com/@drj1189/video/7662131123203443981","isBranded":false},{"id":"7665114040972152077","date":"2026-07-21","thumb":"","title":"Right before Moses stands before Pharaoh, the Bible tells us he’s 80 years old and Aaron is 83. That’s not just a random detail. It’s a reminder that God isn’t in a hurry. Moses spent 40 years in Egypt and another 40 years in the wilderness before stepping into the assignment we remember him for. Your waiting season may not be wasted—it may be preparation for what God has planned all along. #BibleStudy #Exodus7 #Moses #ChristianTok #GodsTiming","views":11470,"videoUrl":"https://www.tiktok.com/@drj1189/video/7665114040972152077","isBranded":false},{"id":"7662113072877702413","date":"2026-07-13","thumb":"","title":"The fact that this documentary could exist says everything. For far too long, many women’s symptoms have been minimized, misattributed, or under-researched. PCOS. Endometriosis. Infertility. Perimenopause. Menopause. Insulin resistance. Metabolic disease. Maternal health. Even heart disease—which often presents differently in women than it does in men. Too many women have been told: “Your labs are normal.” “It’s just anxiety.” “You just need to lose weight.” “Heavy periods are normal.” “Your pain is just part of being a woman.” So they started looking for answers themselves. They searched Google. Reddit. TikTok. Facebook groups. They became experts on their own bodies because they felt like no one else was listening. That shouldn’t be the expectation. Women deserve healthcare that takes their pain seriously. They deserve research that includes them. They deserve clinicians who recognize that heart disease doesn’t always look the same in women, that endometriosis isn’t “just bad cramps,” that infertility is more than a woman’s burden, that maternal health extends far beyond delivery, and that metabolic disease is far more complex than willpower. I became an obesity and lifestyle medicine physician because I wanted to be the doctor who listens, explains the science, and helps women understand what’s actually happening in their bodies. This page is my version of that documentary—evidence-based education for women who’ve ever felt dismissed, confused, or told their symptoms were “just part of being a woman.” Because women deserve to be heard, believed, researched, and cared for. 🩺 Follow for evidence-based content on women’s health, PCOS (PMOS), endometriosis, fertility, pregnancy and postpartum health, menopause, metabolic health, obesity medicine, lifestyle medicine, and GLP-1s. #womenshealth #pcos #pmos #endometriosis #fertility","views":6768,"videoUrl":"https://www.tiktok.com/@drj1189/video/7662113072877702413","isBranded":false}]', '{"topGender":"Female","genderMale":25,"topCountry":"CALIFORNIA","topAgeGroup":"35-44","genderFemale":75,"ageDistribution":[{"name":"35-44","value":28},{"name":"45-54","value":27},{"name":"25-34","value":23},{"name":"55+","value":18},{"name":"18-24","value":4}],"countryDistribution":[{"name":"CALIFORNIA","value":1043},{"name":"TEXAS","value":1004},{"name":"NEW YORK","value":801},{"name":"FLORIDA","value":743},{"name":"GEORGIA","value":611}]}', null, false, null, null, null, null, null, '{"groups":[{"key":"followerTier","items":[{"key":"tier","label":"Follower tier","value":1,"weightPct":10}],"label":"Follower Tier","scorePct":100,"available":true,"weightPct":10},{"key":"gmvPerformance","items":[{"key":"gmvTier","label":"GMV tier so target L3","value":0.65,"weightPct":20},{"key":"gpm","label":"GPM (