Northern California💕🌲', 'https://www.tiktok.com/@smalltowninfluencer', null, 141995, 1466, 9.09, 132.64, 'Food & Beverages', '["Food & Beverages","Toys & Hobbies"]', 74, null, null, 'New Lead', 'Anh Tuan (Scraper Bot)', 'smalltowninfluencer@gmail.com', null, null, null, null, '2026-08-07T08:05:10.189Z', '2026-08-08T17:22:36.301Z', '[]', '["TikTok Scraped","File Import (Kalodata_Creator_20260807160415_US.xlsx)","Scraper Enriched","Pickdi TCM Extension (handle-search)","Pickdi TCM Extension (auto-queue)"]', null, 64, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, '[{"id":"7663233419068902686","date":"2026-07-16","thumb":"","title":"This strawberry pie is one of the best things my aunt ever made!! I have been missing it, but now I have the recipe and so do you!! It tastes like summer. Must serve with freshly whipped cream!! MY AUNT''S FAMOUS STRAWBERRY PIE Crust Ingredients I Cup all-purpose flour ½ cup (1 stick) butter, melted 3 tablespoons sugar ( MY COUSIN MADE ONE AND A HALF''S THE CRUST. I MIGHT TOO BECAUSE IT''S JUST DELICIOUS) Directions Preheat oven to 350°F. Mix the flour, melted butter, and sugar until combined. Pat evenly into a 9-inch pie pan. Bake until lightly golden. Let the crust cool completely, then chill before filling. I like to pop mine in the freezer for about 20 minutes—it works perfectly. Strawberry Filling Ingredients 1 cup sugar 3 tablespoons cornstarch 1 cup water 3 tablespoons strawberry (or raspberry) Jell-O powder 6–8 cups fresh strawberries, hulled and cut in half (or quartered if they''re very large) Directions In a saucepan, whisk together the sugar, cornstarch, and water. Bring to a boil over medium heat, stirring constantly. Cook until the mixture becomes thick and clear. Remove from the heat and stir in the Jell-O until completely dissolved. Let the glaze cool slightly. Assemble Arrange the 6–8 cups of fresh strawberries in the chilled pie crust. Pour the glaze evenly over the strawberries, making sure they''re well coated. Refrigerate for at least 6 hours, or until completely set. Serve chilled with whipped cream. Tips: If your strawberries are especially large, quarter them for easier slicing and better glaze coverage. Chilling the crust in the freezer for about 20 minutes helps keep it crisp, and letting the pie chill for at least 6 hours gives it the perfect texture. #strawberry #strawberrypie","views":193155,"videoUrl":"https://www.tiktok.com/@smalltowninfluencer/video/7663233419068902686","isBranded":false},{"id":"7668885129959378206","date":"2026-08-01","thumb":"","title":"This marinade really did.Give the meat good tenderization and flavor. i would even do it on a ribeye and season.It however I want it after. Next time, the try tip I would definitely do forty minutes. it''s a keeper and a great little thing to have in your back pocket!! thank you  @Spencivetaste for sharing!! so good!! #steak #marinade","views":157164,"videoUrl":"https://www.tiktok.com/@smalltowninfluencer/video/7668885129959378206","isBranded":false},{"id":"7661087818466331935","date":"2026-07-11","thumb":"","title":"Peanut Noodles Remember: 4 tablespoons = ¼ cup. This recipe is for 8 ounces of linguine. (Most linguine is sold in 16-ounce packages, so double the recipe if using the whole package.) Ingredients ¼ cup canola oil 3 tablespoons sesame oil 1 teaspoon red pepper flakes 1 teaspoon salt 3 tablespoons honey 2 tablespoons soy sauce 8 ounces cooked linguine Chopped green onions, to taste Chopped cilantro, to taste ½ cup dry roasted peanuts, crushed Directions Heat the canola oil, sesame oil, and red pepper flakes in a skillet for 2 minutes. Turn off the heat and stir in the salt, honey, and soy sauce. Pour the sauce over the cooked noodles and toss to coat. Add the chopped green onions and cilantro, tossing to combine. Mix ¼ cup of the crushed peanuts into the noodles. Garnish with the remaining crushed peanuts and additional cilantro before serving.  I always make it the day before, and it stays delicious for several days!! #peanutnoodlesalad #pastasalad","views":141187,"videoUrl":"https://www.tiktok.com/@smalltowninfluencer/video/7661087818466331935","isBranded":false}]', '{"topGender":"Female","genderMale":23,"topCountry":"CALIFORNIA","topAgeGroup":"45-54","genderFemale":77,"ageDistribution":[{"name":"45-54","value":33},{"name":"55+","value":32},{"name":"35-44","value":22},{"name":"25-34","value":11},{"name":"18-24","value":2}],"countryDistribution":[{"name":"CALIFORNIA","value":1063},{"name":"TEXAS","value":919},{"name":"NEW YORK","value":632},{"name":"FLORIDA","value":560},{"name":"GEORGIA","value":450}]}', null, false, null, null, null, null, null, '{"groups":[{"key":"followerTier","items":[{"key":"tier","label":"Follower tier","value":1,"weightPct":10}],"label":"Follower Tier","scorePct":100,"available":true,"weightPct":10},{"key":"gmvPerformance","items":[{"key":"gmvTier","label":"GMV tier so target L3","value":0.3,"weightPct":20},{"key":"gpm","label":"GPM (GMV/1000 views, USD)","value":1,"weightPct":15}],"label":"GMV Performance","scorePct":60,"available":true,"weightPct":35},{"key":"audienceProfileFit","items":[{"key":"genderFemale","label":"% nữ trong audience","value":0.85,"weightPct":12},{"key":"preferredAge","label":"% audience ở nhóm tuổi ưu tiên (35-44)","value":0.22,"weightPct":6}],"label":"Audience Profile Fit","scorePct":64,"available":true,"weightPct":30},{"key":"reachConsistency","items":[{"key":"avgViews","label":"Avg views/video","value":1,"weightPct":20}],"label":"Reach Consistency","scorePct":100,"available":true,"weightPct":20}],"scoredAt":"2026-08-08T17:22:36.589Z","riskFlags":[],"strengths":["Follower tier (Follower Tier)","GPM (GMV/1000 views, USD) (GMV Performance)","Avg views/video (Reach Consistency)"],"totalScore":74,"weaknesses":["% audience ở nhóm tuổi ưu tiên (35-44) (Audience Profile Fit)","GMV tier so target L3 (GMV Performance)"],"recommendation":"Priority B - Recommended"}', null, 1786089910189, 33738, 'L1', 29